<title>USA: U.S. oil talks may spur industry action - analysts.</title>
<headline>U.S. oil talks may spur industry action - analysts.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. oil companies might feel compelled to beef up their stocks of heating oil despite the cost after they meet with Energy Secretary Hazel O'Leary on Friday, oil analysts said Thursday.</p>
<p>O'Leary called the meeting last week after Northeastern lawmakers, seeing heating oil stocks at extremely low levels, urged the Energy Department to help stave off a steep jump in heating fuel prices this winter.</p>
<p>Some analysts saw the meeting as a political move by the Clinton administration to avoid offending Northeastern states during the election season and avoid getting into the market.</p>
</text>
